IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wica-types`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — GOAL 7: IS THE EMPLOYER OR PLATFORM
-- OPERATOR PROPERLY INSURED, AND MAY THIS INSURER PROVIDE IT? GOAL 8: WHICH
-- OFFENCE, AND WHAT IS THE MOST THE COURT CAN IMPOSE?
--
-- Part 3 (ss 24-34) and ss 34O-34P; every penalty in the Act with its
-- repeat-offender rule; s 76 (composition); ss 72-73 (officers and partners);
-- s 77; and s 67(4).
--
-- Source: ../source/WICA2019.txt lines 946-1514, 1939-1994, 2057-2073,
-- 2898-2905, 3079-3166, 3385-3404, 3442-3578, 3668-3670.

§ `Goals 7 and 8 — insurance, and offences`

§§ `Goal 7a — must the employer or platform operator be insured, and is it?`

-- s 24(1): every employer "must insure and maintain insurance under one or more
-- approved employee insurance policies with one or more designated employer's
-- insurers against all liabilities ... in respect of every employee", except
-- the excluded classes prescribed under s 24(2)(a). s 34O(1): the same for a
-- platform operator and every platform worker. s 67(4): s 24 does not apply to
-- a seafarer covered by security under the Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour
-- Convention) Act 2014 s 34.
@ref s 24, s 34O, s 67(4)
GIVEN i IS AN `Insurance position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurance duty is met:` i IF
        i's `insured under approved policies with designated insurers for every worker`
    ..  "s 24(2)(a)" ... i's `in an excluded class prescribed under s 24(2)(a)`
    OR  "s 67(4)" ... i's `a seafarer covered by Maritime Labour Convention security`

-- s 25(3), s 34P(3): "It is not a defence ... that the [employer] did not know
-- — (a) the number of [workers] ..., or the extent of [its] liability ...; (b)
-- that any insurance policy ... was not an approved [policy]; or (c) that the
-- insurer was not a designated [insurer], unless the [employer] had taken all
-- reasonable steps to ascertain those matters."
@ref s 25(1), (3); s 34P(1), (3)
GIVEN i IS AN `Insurance position`
      `relies on not knowing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 25(1) / 34P(1) offence is made out on` i `, ignorance pleaded:` `relies on not knowing` IF
        NOT `the insurance duty is met:` i
    AND NOT (`relies on not knowing` AND i's `took all reasonable steps to ascertain the matters in s 25(3)`)

§§ `Goal 7b — the policy (ss 26-27)`

-- s 26(1): an approved policy "(a) must contain all the compulsory terms
-- prescribed ...; and (b) must not contain any term ... that derogates ...
-- from any obligation imposed on the insurer by the compulsory terms".
-- s 26(3): an insurer that issues any policy purporting to insure the
-- liability "is liable to pay that compensation as if the insurance policy
-- contains all the compulsory terms", and a derogating term is void.
-- s 26(4), (4A): not beyond the minimum prescribed under s 24(2)(b) or
-- s 34O(2) (subject to s 47C(4)).
@ref s 26(1)
GIVEN `contains all the compulsory terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contains a derogating term`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an approved policy, compulsory terms:` `contains all the compulsory terms` `, derogating term:` `contains a derogating term` IF
        "(a)" ... `contains all the compulsory terms`
    AND "(b)" ... NOT `contains a derogating term`

@ref s 26(3)-(4A)
GIVEN `the compensation`                 IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed minimum, if any`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the insurer of a purported policy must pay, of compensation` `the compensation` `, the minimum` `the prescribed minimum, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the prescribed minimum, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `the compensation`
    WHEN JUST m   THEN IF `the compensation` GREATER THAN m THEN m ELSE `the compensation`

-- s 27(1): an insurer "is not entitled to raise any objection or defence to a
-- claim on the ground that there is in force another insurance policy ...
-- covering the same liability".
@ref s 27(1)
GIVEN `the defence is double insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may raise the defence, it being double insurance:` `the defence is double insurance` IF
    NOT `the defence is double insurance`

§§ `Goal 7c — the employer becomes insolvent (ss 28-29)`

-- s 28(1): the employer's rights against the insurer "are transferred to and
-- vest in the employee" if "(a) the employer becomes bankrupt or makes a
-- composition or scheme of arrangement ...; (b) where the employer is a
-- company — (i) proceedings are commenced to wind up the company; (ii) a
-- receiver or manager ... is duly appointed; or (iii) possession of any
-- property ... subject to a floating charge ... is taken by ... the holders of
-- the debentures." s 28(5): not on a voluntary winding up only for
-- reconstruction or amalgamation.
-- s 29(2): where the contract is void or voidable for non-compliance (other
-- than premiums), s 28(1) applies only if the employee gives the insurer
-- notice "as soon as practicable" after learning of the injury, the insurance
-- and the insolvency event.
DECLARE `Insolvency facts` HAS
    `bankrupt, or a composition or scheme with creditors`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 28(1)(a)
    `winding-up proceedings commenced`                          IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)
    `a receiver or manager appointed`                           IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)
    `debenture holders took possession under a floating charge` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iii)
    `only a voluntary winding up for reconstruction or amalgamation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (5)
    `the contract is void or voidable other than for premiums`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 29(1)
    `the employee gave the insurer notice as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 29(2)

@ref ss 28(1), (5), 29(1)-(2)
GIVEN f IS AN `Insolvency facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer's rights against the insurer pass to the worker:` f IF
        `an event in (1)`
    AND NOT "(5)" ... f's `only a voluntary winding up for reconstruction or amalgamation`
    AND ((NOT f's `the contract is void or voidable other than for premiums`) OR ("s 29(2)" ... f's `the employee gave the insurer notice as soon as practicable`))
    WHERE
        `an event in (1)` MEANS
                "(a)"     ... f's `bankrupt, or a composition or scheme with creditors`
            ..  "(b)(i)"  ... f's `winding-up proceedings commenced`
            ..  "(b)(ii)" ... f's `a receiver or manager appointed`
            OR  "(b)(iii)" ... f's `debenture holders took possession under a floating charge`

-- s 28(2)(b): the insurer has "the same liabilities ... as if the insurer were
-- the employer, but ... no ... greater liability ... than the insurer's
-- liability to the employer under the contract". s 28(3): the worker may prove
-- for, or recover, the balance.
@ref s 28(2)(b), (3)
GIVEN `the employer's liability`          IS A NUMBER
      `the insurer's liability under the contract` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the balance the worker may prove for, liability` `the employer's liability` `, insurer's liability` `the insurer's liability under the contract` MEANS
    IF   `the employer's liability` GREATER THAN `the insurer's liability under the contract`
    THEN `the employer's liability` MINUS `the insurer's liability under the contract`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Goal 7d — who may provide the insurance (s 30)`

-- s 30(2), (2B): only "(a) a designated [employer's or PO's] insurer that is
-- not suspended under section 31(8)(b) or 34(1)(a); (b) an insurance
-- intermediary in respect of the insurance ... provided ... by [such an]
-- insurer". s 30(3): no one may offer a policy that is not an approved policy.
-- s 30(5): nothing prohibits insurance that does not insure the liability
-- under the Act (health, accident) or insures only liability in excess of it.
@ref s 30(1)-(3), (5)
GIVEN who                       IS A `Kind of provider`
      `an approved policy`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `insures the liability under the Act, beyond any excess-only layer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `providing it is an offence under s 30, provider` who `, approved:` `an approved policy` `, within the Act:` `insures the liability under the Act, beyond any excess-only layer` IF
        "(5)" ... `insures the liability under the Act, beyond any excess-only layer`
    AND (    "(1), (2A)" ... who EQUALS `anyone else`
         OR  "(3)"       ... NOT `an approved policy`)

§§ `Goal 7e — designated insurers (ss 31-34)`

-- s 34(1)(b): a financial penalty "not exceeding $30,000 for each such failure
-- that is not an offence". s 34(5): interest at the judgment-debt rate if
-- unpaid by the date set. s 31(6): a designation expires at the end of the
-- period (if any) the Commissioner specifies, unless cancelled earlier.
@ref s 34(1)(b)
GIVEN failures IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Commissioner may impose on a designated insurer, failures being` failures MEANS
    30000 TIMES failures

@ref s 31(6)
GIVEN `designated until`  IS A MAYBE DATE
      `cancelled on`      IS A MAYBE DATE
      d                   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the designation, until` `designated until` `, cancelled` `cancelled on` `, is in force on` d IF
        `not expired`
    AND `not cancelled`
    WHERE
        `not expired` MEANS
            CONSIDER `designated until`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST e  THEN d AT MOST e
        `not cancelled` MEANS
            CONSIDER `cancelled on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST c  THEN d LESS THAN c

§§ `Goal 8a — the repeat-offender rules`

-- Each offence names the earlier convictions that make a person a repeat
-- offender (ss 25(2), (5); 30(2C), (3A); 34P(2), (5); 35(9); 61(2), (4);
-- 62(2), (4); 68(7)), or speaks of a "second or subsequent conviction"
-- (ss 50(4), 61(5)). Each is encoded as written.
@ref ss 25(2), 25(5), 30(2C), 30(3A), 34P(2), 34P(5), 35(9), 50(4), 61(2), 61(4), 61(5), 62(2), 62(4), 68(7)
GIVEN e   IS AN `Earlier conviction`
      now IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier conviction` e `counts for a repeat of` now IF
    CONSIDER now
    WHEN `s 25(1) — employer not insured` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 25(1) — employer not insured`, `s 34P(1) — platform operator not insured`) OR `repealed` "35(1)(b)"
    WHEN `s 34P(1) — platform operator not insured` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 34P(1) — platform operator not insured`, `s 25(1) — employer not insured`) OR `repealed` "35(1)(b)"
    WHEN `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings`, `s 34P(4) — platform operator deducting insurance cost from earnings`) OR `repealed` "35(1)(a)"
    WHEN `s 34P(4) — platform operator deducting insurance cost from earnings` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 34P(4) — platform operator deducting insurance cost from earnings`, `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings`) OR `repealed` "35(1)(a)"
    WHEN `s 30(1) — unauthorised provider of employer insurance` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 30(1) — unauthorised provider of employer insurance`, `s 30(2A) — unauthorised provider of platform operator insurance`)
    WHEN `s 30(2A) — unauthorised provider of platform operator insurance` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 30(1) — unauthorised provider of employer insurance`, `s 30(2A) — unauthorised provider of platform operator insurance`)
    WHEN `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy`)
    WHEN `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident`) OR e's `under the old regulation 3(5)`
    WHEN `s 50(4) — failing to comply with a direction` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 50(4) — failing to comply with a direction`)
    WHEN `s 61(1) — failing to pay compensation` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 61(1) — failing to pay compensation`) OR `repealed` "35(2)(a)"
    WHEN `s 61(3) — failing to deposit interest` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 61(3) — failing to deposit interest`) OR `repealed` "35(2)(b)"
    WHEN `s 61(5) — failing to make a directed deposit` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 61(5) — failing to make a directed deposit`)
    WHEN `s 62(1) — false or misleading information` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 62(1) — false or misleading information`) OR `repealed` "35(2)(c)"
    WHEN `s 62(3)(a) — dishonestly obtaining compensation` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 62(3)(a) — dishonestly obtaining compensation`, `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation`) OR `repealed` "35(2)(f)"
    WHEN `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 62(3)(a) — dishonestly obtaining compensation`, `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation`)
    WHEN `s 68(6) — obstructing the Commissioner or an investigation officer` THEN
        `one of` (LIST `s 68(6) — obstructing the Commissioner or an investigation officer`) OR `repealed` "35(2)(e)"
    WHEN `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations` THEN FALSE
    WHERE
        `one of` offences MEANS (NOT e's `under the repealed Act`) AND (NOT e's `under the old regulation 3(5)`) AND elem (e's `offence`) offences
        `repealed` provision MEANS e's `under the repealed Act` AND e's `repealed Act provision` EQUALS provision

@ref as above
GIVEN now     IS AN Offence
      earlier IS A LIST OF `Earlier conviction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a repeat offender for` now `, with earlier convictions` earlier IF
    any (GIVEN e YIELD `an earlier conviction` e `counts for a repeat of` now) earlier

§§ `Goal 8b — the maximum penalty`

-- Each offence's ceiling, first and repeat. For s 30 the fine is per insurance
-- policy (ss 30(1), (2A), (3)). s 82(3): regulations may make contravention an
-- offence punishable up to $10,000, 6 months or both — a ceiling on the
-- regulations, with no repeat tier.
@ref ss 25(1), 25(4), 30(1), 30(2A), 30(3), 34P(1), 34P(4), 35(8), 50(4), 61(1), 61(3), 61(5), 62(1), 62(3), 68(6), 82(3)
GIVEN o      IS AN Offence
      repeat IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`the maximum penalty for` o `, a repeat offender:` repeat MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    --                                                                                          first             repeat
    WHEN `s 25(1) — employer not insured`                                         THEN `tier` 10000 12        20000 12
    WHEN `s 34P(1) — platform operator not insured`                               THEN `tier` 10000 12        20000 12
    WHEN `s 25(4) — employer deducting insurance cost from earnings`              THEN `tier`  5000  6        10000  6
    WHEN `s 34P(4) — platform operator deducting insurance cost from earnings`    THEN `tier`  5000  6        10000  6
    WHEN `s 30(1) — unauthorised provider of employer insurance`                  THEN `tier` 80000  0       160000  0
    WHEN `s 30(2A) — unauthorised provider of platform operator insurance`        THEN `tier` 80000  0       160000  0
    WHEN `s 30(3) — insurance that is not an approved policy`                     THEN `tier` 80000  0       160000  0
    WHEN `s 35(8) — failing to give the Commissioner notice of an accident`       THEN `tier`  5000  0        10000  6
    WHEN `s 50(4) — failing to comply with a direction`                           THEN `tier`  5000  6        10000  6
    WHEN `s 61(1) — failing to pay compensation`                                  THEN `tier` 15000 12        30000 12
    WHEN `s 61(3) — failing to deposit interest`                                  THEN `tier` 15000 12        30000 12
    WHEN `s 61(5) — failing to make a directed deposit`                           THEN `tier` 15000 12        30000 12
    WHEN `s 62(1) — false or misleading information`                              THEN `tier`  5000  6        10000  6
    WHEN `s 62(3)(a) — dishonestly obtaining compensation`                        THEN `tier` 15000 12        30000 12
    WHEN `s 62(3)(b) — dishonestly avoiding liability to pay compensation`        THEN `tier` 15000 12        30000 12
    WHEN `s 68(6) — obstructing the Commissioner or an investigation officer`     THEN `tier`  5000  6        10000  6
    WHEN `s 82(3) — contravening the regulations`                                 THEN `tier` 10000  6        10000  6
    WHERE
        `tier` f1 m1 f2 m2 MEANS
            IF repeat THEN `Maximum penalty` OF f2, m2 ELSE `Maximum penalty` OF f1, m1

§§ `Goal 8c — composition, officers, and the Government`

-- s 76(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of ... (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine
-- that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000." Which offences are
-- compoundable is prescribed by regulations: an input.
@ref s 76(1)
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition limit for an offence with a maximum fine of` `the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2 LESS THAN 5000 THEN `the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE 5000

-- ss 72(2), 73(2): where a corporation (or an unincorporated association or
-- partnership) commits an offence, an officer, partner or manager in a
-- position to influence its conduct who "(i) consented or connived, or
-- conspired ...; (ii) is ... knowingly concerned in, or is party to, the
-- commission of the offence ...; or (iii) knew or ought reasonably to have
-- known that the offence ... would be or is being committed, and failed to
-- take all reasonable steps to prevent or stop [it]" is guilty of the same
-- offence. ss 72(3), 73(3): with the body's defences.
DECLARE `Officer facts` HAS
    `an officer, partner, or manager able to influence the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consented, connived or conspired`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `knowingly concerned in or party to it`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or ought to have known, and did not take all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 72(2), 73(2)
GIVEN f                    IS AN `Officer facts`
      `the body committed it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty of the same offence:` f `, the body having committed it:` `the body committed it` IF
        `the body committed it`
    AND "(a)" ... f's `an officer, partner, or manager able to influence the conduct`
    AND "(b)" ... (    "(i)"   ... f's `consented, connived or conspired`
                   ..  "(ii)"  ... f's `knowingly concerned in or party to it`
                   OR  "(iii)" ... f's `knew or ought to have known, and did not take all reasonable steps`)

-- s 77: "nothing in this Act renders the Government liable to prosecution".
@ref s 77
GIVEN `the accused is the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be prosecuted under the Act, the accused being the Government:` `the accused is the Government` IF
    NOT `the accused is the Government`
